# .dockerignore - files Docker leaves out when it builds the image (the "build context").
#
# Leaving them out makes builds faster and keeps secrets out of the image:
# - .env: API keys are passed in at run time by docker-compose.yml, never baked into the image.
# - .git, .venv, __pycache__: history and local caches the app does not need.
# - infra: Terraform files (Phase 5), used from your machine or CI only.
# - evals/audio: large test recordings.

.env
.git
.venv
__pycache__
infra
evals/audio
